cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MIDAS in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MIDAS: Mineral Interface Dynamics and apparent-Age Simulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Stroh
    given-names: Annalena
    affiliation: "Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz (JGU)"
  - family-names: Moulas
    given-names: Evangelos
    affiliation: "Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz (JGU)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnStroh/MIDAS"
abstract: >
  MIDAS is an interface-limited crystal-growth model (a moving-boundary
  problem) for a garnet crystal growing/resorbing in a matrix, coupled to
  major-element (Mg-Fe-Mn) and trace-element (Lu, Hf, Mn) diffusion and
  partitioning - built for modeling Lu-Hf garnet geochronology. Provided as
  MATLAB, GNU Octave, and interactive GUI (MATLAB App Designer) versions.
keywords:
  - geochronology
  - Lu-Hf
  - garnet
  - crystal growth
  - Stefan problem
  - moving boundary
  - diffusion
  - petrology
